        kind: 'worked',
        text: 'A bent steel bracket: steel €2.40 per part including offcuts; laser cutting 1.2 minutes and press brake (the machine that bends the sheet) 1.8 minutes, both at €80 per hour; setups take 1 hour in total per batch at €80 per hour; batch 50; 3% scrap at final inspection; overhead surcharge 15% on the total. Sales says the customer will pay €8.50 per part.\n\nBuild it line by line. Machine time: 3.0 minutes at €80 per hour = €4.00. Setup: €80 / 50 = €1.60. Material + machine + setup = €8.00. With 3% late scrap: €8.00 / 0.97 = €8.25. Plus 15% overhead: €9.48.\n\nAt €8.50 this order loses money at a batch of 50. At a batch of 200, setup drops to €0.40, the sum to €6.80, with scrap €7.01, with overhead €8.06: then it earns.\n\nSo the real question for sales: what batch size and yearly volume will the customer commit to, for example as call-offs, firm orders of 200 at a time under a yearly agreement?',
