        text: 'A maker of hydraulic cylinders has a setup pool of €240,000 a year (setters, first-part checks) for 1,200 setups. Today that setup cost sits in the overhead, spread at €6 per direct labour hour. A standard cylinder takes 1.0 labour hour and is made in batches of 500; a special takes 1.5 hours and comes in batches of 10. Sales says specials are the most profitable line.',
        ask: 'What setup cost does each cylinder carry now, and what would ABC give?',
